    "en":  {
               "headline":  "AXON at two-year lows after Q3 miss, Dedrone delays and $1.2B Skydio bet",
               "technical":  "The trend is clearly down. At USD 291.14, the price is below all three exponential moving averages (EMAs, which give more weight to recent prices): EMA50 at 395.64, EMA100 at 437.16 and EMA200 at 476.47. They are stacked in fully bearish order, with the shortest on the bottom, and the price is about 26% below EMA50. Momentum is still negative. MACD (a trend-momentum gauge built from two moving averages) is at -34.49, below its signal line at -30.99, so the histogram is -3.5. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 27.93, which says the stock is oversold, but oversold readings can last a long time in a downtrend. The Bollinger Bands (a 20-day average ± 2 standard deviations) are very wide, from 240.48 to 474.41 around a 357.44 middle, which reflects how violent the selloff has been. The price sits in the lower half of the bands, not yet at the lower band. On 20 Nov the stock touched 325.90 intraday but closed near its low of 289.69, a new 52-week low and 56% below the 665.07 high. Volume of 2.08M was 1.21x the 20-day average, so sellers were in control.",
               "fundamental":  "Axon\u0027s software side still looks strong. In Q3 2026 (results released 5 Nov), annual recurring revenue (ARR) was USD 1.75B (+40%), net revenue retention (revenue from existing customers vs a year earlier) was 126%, and future contracted bookings were USD 15.8B (+39%). Software \u0026 Services grew 43% to USD 437M, and AI ARR passed USD 100M. The weak spots were elsewhere. Total revenue of USD 909M (+28%) missed consensus. Connected Devices growth slowed to 16%, and TASER and body cameras came in slightly below forecasts. GAAP gross margin fell to 56.7% from 60.1%, hit by counter-drone product mix and higher memory-chip costs. FY2026 revenue guidance was cut to USD 3.61–3.63B (~30% growth, from 32–34%). Free-cash-flow guidance fell to USD 350–400M from 450M, and debt (USD 2.97B) now exceeds cash (USD 1.66B).",
               "news":  [
                            "5 Nov 2026: Q3 revenue of USD 909M and adjusted EPS of USD 1.72 both missed estimates. Axon took about USD 130M of federal Dedrone counter-drone deployments out of its 2026 outlook and cut full-year growth guidance to ~30%.",
                            "5 Nov 2026: Axon announced an additional USD 1.2B investment in drone maker Skydio, lifting its fully diluted stake to about 37% and making it Skydio\u0027s exclusive US/Canada public-safety distributor. A later filing indicates roughly 90% will be paid in cash.",
                            "6 Nov 2026: The stock fell about 18% in one session, the S\u0026P 500\u0027s biggest decliner that day and Axon\u0027s lowest level since August 2024. Piper Sandler called it \u0027arguably Axon\u0027s worst quarter as a public company\u0027 but said it does not believe Axon has lost business.",
                            "6 Nov 2026: Craig-Hallum downgraded the stock to Hold (target USD 390). Raymond James (to 475 from 675), JPMorgan (to 610 from 755), Northland (to 540 from 800) and others cut their targets but kept positive ratings.",
                            "20 Nov 2026: Shares fell another 5.2% to USD 291.14, a fresh 52-week low, with no new company-specific news found. It looks like the post-earnings selloff continuing."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The chart has not shown any sign of bottoming. Price is far below every EMA, MACD is still under its signal, and the 20 Nov close came at a new low on above-average volume. An oversold RSI alone is not a buy signal in a strong downtrend. On the business side, cash is getting tighter: free cash flow is lower, net debt has risen, and the Skydio deal is mostly paid in cash. Federal counter-drone revenue has proved lumpy and hard to time, and investors may stay doubtful until the Q4 report in February 2027.",
               "opportunity":  "The parts of Axon that drive long-term value held up. ARR grew 40%, customers spent 26% more than a year earlier, and the USD 15.8B contracted backlog rose 39%. The guidance cut was about federal deployment timing, not lost customers, and analysts who cut targets mostly kept Buy-type ratings. If the delayed Dedrone projects land in 2027 and Skydio deepens the drone-as-first-responder platform, today\u0027s discount to the 52-week high could later look like an overreaction. The 240–290 zone (lower band and 52-week low) is the nearest support area to watch.",
               "risks":  [
                             "The three delayed federal Dedrone deployments (~USD 130M) could slip further or shrink.",
                             "Gross-margin pressure from counter-drone hardware mix and rising memory-chip costs.",
                             "Balance-sheet strain: debt above cash, free cash flow cut and a mostly cash-funded USD 1.2B Skydio stake.",
                             "Hardware softness: TASER and body-camera sales came in slightly below forecasts.",
                             "Valuation is still high (around 96x trailing earnings per Trefis), so further estimate cuts could hurt the stock more."
                         ],
               "summary":  "AXON is in a confirmed downtrend. All EMAs sit above the price in bearish order, MACD is negative, and the stock closed 20 Nov at a 52-week low of about USD 291 on heavy volume, although RSI 27.93 shows it is oversold. The news explains the move: a Q3 miss, about USD 130M of delayed federal Dedrone revenue, a lower cash outlook and a costly Skydio bet. The core software moat (ARR +40%, NRR 126%, USD 15.8B backlog) looks intact. Hardware execution and capital allocation now need close watching."
